From 9dc66e497a0de5d5e83371b6f17840f139c9246a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bpu-verify <bpu-verify@local>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 18:59:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(mbtb): qualify direction-counter update by tag hit

MainBtbAlignBank updated a way's direction counter whenever the stored
7-bit position equalled the trained branch's cfiPosition, without
requiring the entry's tag to match. A set conflict that leaves another
block in the same way with an equal position therefore fed this branch's
outcome into a foreign entry's counter, corrupting that branch's
direction history and, through later predictions, its target/position.

The entry-write path (t1_hitMask) and the replacer touch
(t1_actualTakenMask) already require the tag hit; only the counter update
skipped it. Qualify the counter hit mask with meta.rawHit as well.

Found by tests/bpu/testcase/test_ahead_working_set.py and
test_main_cold_original_order.py, whose checkers name the invariant
"requires original hit": the DUT proposed a direction for a way that
never hit.
---
 .../xiangshan/frontend/bpu/mbtb/MainBtbAlignBank.scala | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/main/scala/xiangshan/frontend/bpu/mbtb/MainBtbAlignBank.scala b/src/main/scala/xiangshan/frontend/bpu/mbtb/MainBtbAlignBank.scala
index 240d92171..df473e552 100644
--- a/src/main/scala/xiangshan/frontend/bpu/mbtb/MainBtbAlignBank.scala
+++ b/src/main/scala/xiangshan/frontend/bpu/mbtb/MainBtbAlignBank.scala
@@ -256,8 +256,16 @@ class MainBtbAlignBank(
   private val t1_counterWayMask = Wire(Vec(NumWay, Bool()))
 
   t1_meta.zipWithIndex.foreach { case (meta, i) =>
+    // A direction counter belongs to the entry that stores it. Matching the
+    // three-bit position alone is not enough: another block may occupy this way
+    // in the same set with an equal position, and feeding this branch's outcome
+    // into that entry's counter would corrupt a foreign identity. `rawHit` is
+    // the entry's tag match, i.e. "this way holds *this* block"; the entry-write
+    // path below (`t1_hitMask`) and the replacer touch (`t1_actualTakenMask`)
+    // already qualify the same way.
     val hitMask = t1_branches.map { branch =>
-      branch.valid && branch.bits.attribute.isConditional && meta.position === branch.bits.cfiPosition
+      branch.valid && branch.bits.attribute.isConditional && meta.rawHit &&
+        meta.position === branch.bits.cfiPosition
     }
     val actualTaken = Mux1H(hitMask, t1_branches.map(_.bits.taken))
 
